How to apply each kind:
- experiment_alternatives: add to the decisive experiment the arm, control or measurement that tells the hypothesis apart
  from each named alternative, and say which result would rule the alternative out.
- rewrite_refuted_link: restate that step of the mechanism so that it no longer claims what the facts against show; narrow
  it to the conditions of the facts for, or replace it by another step the facts support.
- narrow_population: restrict the population of the hypothesis (and of its experiment) to the one the facts for come from.
- write_mechanism: state, as separate steps, how the intervention acts on the outcome (target, pathway, intermediate
  effect); each step must be a claim that can fail on its own. Base the steps on the parent text and the facts; when they
  name no mechanism, state the most direct one the parent text implies and do not invent findings.
- clinical_endpoint: make the primary outcome a functional or clinical measure (performance test, falls, hospital
  admission) instead of a biomarker or a questionnaire; keep the old one as secondary.

Rules: keep the same intervention and the same broad population (unless narrow_population says otherwise); never state a
result as established; the text must read as a registered trial description.

